-- title:
--   Modular function field is finite separable over K(j)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and $N$ a positive natural number with $(N:K)\neq 0$. Inside the field of Laurent series $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,K$ consider the element $\bar\jmath=\mathtt{jqModC}\,K$, namely $q^{-1}$ times the image in $K$ of the integral power series $E_4^3\cdot\eta^{-\text{unit}}$ (`jNum`), and its $N$-fold substitution $\bar\jmath_N=\mathtt{jqNModC}\,K\,N$ obtained by applying `qExpand K N` to $\bar\jmath$; let $F_N=\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\,K\,N$ be the intermediate field $K(\bar\jmath,\bar\jmath_N)$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,K$ over $K$ generated by these two elements. The assertion is the existence of an algebra structure of $F_N$ over the rational function field $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,K$ such that, simultaneously: the tower $K\subseteq\mathrm{RatFunc}\,K\subseteq F_N$ is a scalar tower; the structure map sends the variable $\mathtt{RatFunc.X}$ to the element $\bar\jmath$ of $F_N$ (i.e. $T\mapsto\bar\jmath$); $F_N$ is a finite module over $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,K$; and the extension $F_N/\mathrm{RatFunc}\,K$ is separable. The algebra datum is packaged existentially together with these four properties, so that consumers may install it as a local instance.
--
--   This is the algebraic form of the classical statement that the level-$N$ modular function field $K(j,j_N)$ is a finite separable extension of the rational function field $K(j)$, valid over any base field in which $N$ is invertible. It supplies the function-field hypotheses (finiteness and separability over $K(T)$) used by the residue-theorem and Riemann–Roch inputs for modular curves, and is invoked in the treatment of places and branch points on the models of $X_0(N)$ and of full level structure.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_algebra_ratFunc_modularFunctionFieldC_finite_isSeparable.lean

